// A tree changed from inside `for`s that cascade along it (Inputs/
// tree_grow.ent): nodes spawned and connected, a component added and
// removed, which moves the nodes between two archetypes, and edges
// disconnected. Each takes effect when its `for` has run. Sorted, across
// the two archetypes, the tree gives the same lines.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/tree_grow.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.out
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/tree_grow.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: sed 's/ tree capacity 32/ tree sorted capacity 32/' \
// RUN:     %S/Inputs/tree_grow.ent > %t.sorted.ent
// RUN: grep -q "tree sorted" %t.sorted.ent
// RUN: %ent run %t.sorted.ent 2>/dev/null | sort > %t.sorted.out
// RUN: sort %t.out | cmp - %t.sorted.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out

// CHECK:      1: root depth 0 total 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: a depth 1 total 11
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: b depth 1 total 101
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: c depth 2 total 1011
// A new node under c, the one node of depth 2: there, but not in the tree
// while the `for` that made it ran.
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: root depth 0 total 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: a depth 1 total 11
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: b depth 1 total 101
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: c depth 2 total 1011
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: bud depth 0 total 0
// It is under c now; c and it are flagged, and in the other archetype.
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: root depth 0 total 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: a depth 1 total 11
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: b depth 1 total 101
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: bud depth 3 total 1016 flagged in 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: c depth 2 total 1011 flagged in 3
// And back.
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: root depth 0 total 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: a depth 1 total 11
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: b depth 1 total 101
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: c depth 2 total 1011
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: bud depth 3 total 1016
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: root depth 0 total 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: a depth 1 total 11
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: b depth 1 total 101
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: c depth 2 total 1011
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: bud depth 3 total 1016
// a and b have let go of the root.
// CHECK-NEXT: 6: root depth 0 total 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 6: a depth 0 total 10
// CHECK-NEXT: 6: b depth 0 total 100
// CHECK-NEXT: 6: c depth 1 total 1010
// CHECK-NEXT: 6: bud depth 2 total 1015
// CHECK-NOT:  {{.}}
